B.by3=new A.lI(B.yz,B.ow,"Opening Balance (Carry Fwd.)",'Represents all transactions from months BEFORE your selected date range.\n\nHow it works:\n1. At month end (e.g. 30 Apr), set the date range to that exact month.\n2. Click "Save Snapshot" in the GST Reconciliation tab.\n3. Next time you view May, the April snapshot appears as the opening row.\n4. Totals row = opening carry-fwd + current period.\n\nNo snapshot \u2192 row is hidden and a warning banner appears.\nData added after snapshot \u2192 \u26a0 badge appears. Click "Recreate Snapshot" to refresh.')
B.aeo=new A.ag(61214,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a8h=new A.I(1,0.47058823529411764,0.20784313725490197,0.058823529411764705,B.C)
B.by_=new A.lI(B.aeo,B.a8h,"Snapshots \u2014 What, Why, When","A snapshot is a frozen copy of a month's totals saved to Firestore.\n\nWhy: Rather than re-querying all past bills on every load, the snapshot captures final totals once and reads them instantly.\n\nWhen to save: Only after a month is fully closed. Cannot snapshot the current month.\n\nStaleness: If you add a transaction dated inside an already-snapshotted month, it becomes stale (\u26a0). Recreate it to include the new data.\n\nSchema: Amounts are stored by GST rate slab dynamically (byRate map), so all future rate additions are supported automatically.")
B.a96=new A.I(1,0.054901960784313725,0.4549019607843137,0.5647058823529412,B.C)
B.by1=new A.lI(B.Ij,B.a96,"How Net GST Payable is Calculated","Net GST Payable = Output GST (Sales) \u2212 Input GST (Purchases / ITC)\n\nComponent-wise:\n\u2022 Net IGST = Sales IGST \u2212 Purchase IGST\n\u2022 Net CGST = Sales CGST \u2212 Purchase CGST\n\u2022 Net SGST = Sales SGST \u2212 Purchase SGST\n\nNegative means ITC > output tax for that slab \u2014 the excess can offset other components per GST rules.\n\nSummary card = period only. GST Reconciliation Combined row adds the opening carry-fwd for the full picture.")
